  "surprise": "Late-phase SAM (rho 0.05, last 25% of the wall-clock) on 153-claude scored 650/678/649 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 676/700/685: exact means 659.00 vs 687.00, -28.0, paired -26/-22/-36, inside the registered -35..+30 but far below its central -2. Discard. The mechanism ran as registered. Steps were 3907/3759/3916 (mean 3861 vs 153's 4503, -14%; inside 3,700-4,250), with sam_steps 625/609/625 at ~8.3 steps/s in the window vs ~15.9 before it. The sharpness proxy (sam_loss - train_loss) fell on every seed from the first to the last SAM curve point (0.0032->0.0021, 0.0068->0.0023, 0.0128->0.0024), so the handoff did sit in a flatter region by this measure. The registered RL falsifier fired: round-1 targets solved were 670/693/642 vs 153's 766/747/694, lower on all three seeds (round-1 sample acc 0.241/0.209/0.226 vs 153 s0 0.271), and round 4 reached 1121/1164/1082 (153 s0: 1157). Surprise: pretraining again looked better while RL got worse. Final main val loss was 0.0787/0.0823/0.0846 vs 153's 0.088/0.087/0.089, and eval held-out greedy was 0.989/0.989/0.990. That is the pattern of 158 (width 448), 167 (12 heads) and 170 (statement ALiBi): lower in-distribution loss with worse round-1 coverage. It suggests the round-1 pass@32 on longer targets is what binds, and that flatness at this rho does not buy it. Unmeasured confound: the 14% fewer steps.",
